      "block_id": "2605.24856_p14_b0",
      "text": "Figure 1: Single-region detection (left) versus scored CAZ profile (right). The single-region detector\nbrackets one allocation zone around the global separation peak for sentiment in Pythia-1.4B (peak\nL10, 42% depth). The scored detector, applied to temporal_order in the same model, resolves\ntwo CAZes at geometrically distinct depths (\u00a74.5): a shallow strong CAZ (L4, 17% depth, score\n0.47) and a deep major CAZ (L12, 50% depth, score 0.65) \u2014 the single-region method would\nbracket only the deeper peak and miss the shallow one. N=250 contrastive pairs, w = 3 velocity\nsmoothing (diagnostic only), final-token probing, scored detection defaults (0.5% prominence floor,\n3% valley-merge threshold).\n",
      "bbox": [
        71.73,
        258.19,
        541.72,
        363.94
      ],
      "rendered_bbox": [
        286,
        1032,
        2166,
        1455
      ],
