    {
      "block_id": "2605.24856_p14_b3",
      "text": "Scored Detection\nThe prominence-based detector requires a threshold to determine which\npeaks are significant. A fixed threshold (e.g., 10% of global max separation) is arbitrary and risks\ndiscarding subtle but causally active allocation regions. We replace it with a composite scoring\nsystem:\n",
